                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I do not precisely remember why I put this game two years ago in the shooter/action/whatever folder of my Steam library..\nBeing 50mbs heavy, it surely can't offer something great but I'm always the guy who doesn't give a fuck about graphic quality and such!\nThough, reading \"Otakumaker\" in the editor field scares me a bit..\nMade with the Unity engine, as usual you can choose between lots of windowed resolution, graphic settings and such before starting the game.\nWhich opens up with a non-exciting MS Paint purple circle and some kind of text, a play button, max level and highscore. That's all.\nThe game offers absolutely no help section, no tutorial, literally nothing - pushing play will put you inside the only level this game offers, and you'll be literally a yellow rectangular bar within some kind of first-person space setting.\nYou will have to find out that you are forced to actually spin around that yellow thing and you can't move it in the four directions - the left directional key will make it form a clockwise circle and the right key the opposite.\nThis is it.\nAnd the whole game is made up by other tunnels (purple circles) in which you're supposed to enter matching the yellow color with the yellow part in said circles.\nI highly doubt this game will stay here forever, but anyways for anyone out there - don't buy this thing. It's just an asset flip - you're in space, and you'll command a yellow thing trying to match other yellow circles. This is literally the whole game.\nIt is also superfluous and pointless to add that, since this game has been made within 5 minutes, it has no interface or user-friendly options - you'll simply die upon the first wrong touch and be transported to the beginning, nothing more.\nUntil it gets removed from Steam this thing has to be avoided at all costs.",
